RUN: %PLC -c --fpic %S/interface_dispatch_lib.st -o %t.lib.o
RUN: %COMPILE -i %S/interface_dispatch_lib.st %S/interface_dispatch_main.st %t.lib.o && %RUN | %CHECK %s

interface_dispatch_lib.st declares interfaces and function blocks, and is
compiled to its own object. The program includes it, links that object, and
dispatches through the interfaces in both directions: it calls library types
through interfaces, and the library calls program types that implement library
interfaces. ILogger has no implementor in the library, so only the object built
from interface_dispatch_lib.st may define its interface table type.

